# Python bytecode + test caches from the wizard compose harnesses
# (_fragments/_tools/*.py) and the language-fragment skeletons (e.g.
# _fragments/backend/fastapi/skeleton). These must never be committed: the
# compose action (capstone:compose-project) nunjucks-renders every non-verbatim
# fragment file, and a binary .pyc containing `{%` bytes crashes the render
# ("tag name expected"), breaking Python scaffolds. See composeProject.ts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
